{
  "number": 4,
  "meaning": "Universality and the Created",
  "description": "The number four represents the created world and its universal extent. There are four corners of the earth, four winds, and four seasons. In Eden's garden, the river divided into four branches (Gen 2:10). Ezekiel's vision contains four living creatures with four faces and four wings, representing all creation (Ezek 1:5–6). These four beings reappear in Revelation as the four living creatures around God's throne (Rev 4:6–8). In the New Testament, Jesus sends his disciples to all four corners of the earth, and the four gospels carry the message to the whole world.",
